      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bremen%2C_Kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early settlers from Germany established the community around 1832, drawn by the region's fertile farmland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kyatlas.com/ky-bremen.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office called Bremen has been in operation since 1832, serving as the town's first permanent institution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bremen%2C_Kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bremen was formally incorporated as a home rule-class city on March 12, 1869.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
